WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.288 --> 00:00:02.989
I would name you
the Hand of the King.

2
00:00:03.023 --> 00:00:06.459
<i>I have a son. you have a daughter.</i>
<i>we'll join our houses.</i>

3
00:00:07.661 --> 00:00:10.364
May I present Viserys
of House Targaryen

4
00:00:10.398 --> 00:00:12.599
<i>and his sister</i>
<i>Daenerys?</i>

5
00:00:12.634 --> 00:00:15.636
I give him a queen
and he gives me an army.

6
00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:17.437
( Moaning )

7
00:00:17.471 --> 00:00:20.107
- ( Gasps )
- Maester says the boy may live.

8
00:00:20.141 --> 00:00:23.078
My dear brother. there are times you
make me wonder whose side you're on.

9
00:00:23.145 --> 00:00:24.845
You know how much
I love my family.

10
00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:26.881
There's great honor serving
in the Night's Watch.

11
00:00:26.915 --> 00:00:28.283
<i>The Starks have</i>
<i>manned the wall</i>

12
00:00:28.317 --> 00:00:30.652
<i>for thousands of years.</i>
<i>And you are a Stark.</i>

13
00:00:30.686 --> 00:00:34.289
<i>King Robert's bastards--</i>
<i>Jon Arryn tracked them all down. Why?</i>

14
00:00:34.323 --> 00:00:36.625
<i>The King has</i>
<i>no trueborn sons.</i>

15
00:00:36.659 --> 00:00:38.427
- Do you love your children?
- With all my heart.

16
00:00:38.461 --> 00:00:40.729
- No more than I love mine.
- <i>And they're all Jaime's.</i>

17
00:00:40.763 --> 00:00:43.666
Ned: <i>When the King returns from</i>
<i>his hunt. I'll tell him the truth.</i>

18
00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:46.802
I want what I came for. I want
the crown he promised me.

19
00:00:46.836 --> 00:00:49.138
- No! No!
- A crown for a king.

20
00:00:49.173 --> 00:00:51.407
- ( Screaming )
- Daenerys: <i>He was no dragon.</i>

21
00:00:51.442 --> 00:00:54.244
- Fire cannot kill the dragon.
- ( Clangs )

22
00:00:54.278 --> 00:00:56.379
Aemon: <i>Jon Snow.</i>
<i>Lord Commander Mormont</i>

23
00:00:56.413 --> 00:00:59.014
<i>has requested you</i>
<i>for his personal steward.</i>

24
00:00:59.049 --> 00:01:01.283
He wants to groom you
for command.

25
00:01:01.317 --> 00:01:02.884
Renly:
Ned! We were hunting.

26
00:01:02.919 --> 00:01:06.054
By the time Robert dies. it will be
too late for the both of us.

27
00:01:06.088 --> 00:01:07.989
What about Stannis?
He's your older brother.

28
00:01:08.023 --> 00:01:09.990
<i>This isn't about the bloody</i>
<i>line of succession.</i>

29
00:01:10.025 --> 00:01:11.892
He's not a king.
I am.

30
00:01:11.926 --> 00:01:14.895
- We have a new king now.
- Your son has no claim to the throne.

31
00:01:14.929 --> 00:01:17.330
Kill him! Kill all of them!
I command it!

32
00:01:17.364 --> 00:01:20.833
You're summoned to King's Landing
to swear fealty to the new king.

33
00:01:20.867 --> 00:01:23.635
Joffrey puts my father in chains;
Now he wants his ass kissed?

34
00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:25.971
I'll go to King's Landing.
but not alone.

35
00:01:26.005 --> 00:01:28.440
<i>Call the Banners.</i>

36
00:01:28.475 --> 00:01:31.344
- Theon: <i>Kill him. Robb.</i>
- He's more use to us alive than dead.

37
00:01:31.378 --> 00:01:33.813
- <i>( Crowd shouting )</i>
- So long as I am your king.

38
00:01:33.848 --> 00:01:36.383
<i>treason shall never</i>
<i>go unpunished.</i>

39
00:01:36.417 --> 00:01:38.518
- No! No!
- Stop. my son.

40
00:01:38.553 --> 00:01:39.986
You will go
to King's Landing

41
00:01:40.021 --> 00:01:42.155
and serve as Hand
of the King in my stead.

42
00:01:42.189 --> 00:01:45.792
<i>You'll bring that boy king to heel.</i>
<i>and his mother. too. if needs be.</i>

43
00:01:45.826 --> 00:01:47.627
Please let me go home.

44
00:01:47.661 --> 00:01:49.528
Mother says I'm still
to marry you.

45
00:01:49.563 --> 00:01:51.831
so you'll stay here
and obey.

46
00:01:52.999 --> 00:01:55.133
My sword is yours
in victory and defeat.

47
00:01:55.168 --> 00:01:58.903
All: The King in the North!
The King in the North!

48
00:01:58.938 --> 00:02:00.038
What's your name?

49
00:02:00.072 --> 00:02:01.539
- Arry.
- Arry the orphan boy.

50
00:02:01.574 --> 00:02:04.610
It's 1.000 leagues
from here to the Wall.

51
00:02:04.644 --> 00:02:06.678
We ride out
beyond the Wall tomorrow.

52
00:02:06.713 --> 00:02:08.647
<i>The Night's Watch</i>
<i>will ride in force</i>

53
00:02:08.681 --> 00:02:10.882
<i>against the wildlings.</i>
<i>the White Walkers.</i>

54
00:02:10.916 --> 00:02:12.483
<i>and whatever else</i>
<i>is out there.</i>

55
00:02:12.518 --> 00:02:15.286
- He will die tonight. Khaleesi.
- ( Sobbing )

56
00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:18.623
Drogo will have no use for
dragon eggs in the Night Lands.

57
00:02:18.658 --> 00:02:20.859
You don't understand.

58
00:02:22.428 --> 00:02:24.463
Blood of my blood.

59
00:02:24.497 --> 00:02:26.431
( Hisses )

60
00:02:26.465 --> 00:02:29.234
( Screeches )

61
00:02:36.744 --> 00:02:39.279
<i>( Theme music playing )</i>

62
00:02:39.304 --> 00:02:43.304
<font color=#00FF00>♪ Game of Thrones 2x01 ♪</font>
<font color=#00FFFF>The North Remembers</font>
Original Air Date on April 1. 2012

63
00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:47.329
== sync. corrected by <font color="#00ff00">elderman</font> ==

64
00:04:24.651 --> 00:04:26.886
( Both yelling )

65
00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:41.868
( Applause. cheering )

66
00:04:41.902 --> 00:04:44.337
Well struck.

67
00:04:44.371 --> 00:04:46.139
Well struck. Dog.

68
00:04:49.943 --> 00:04:51.878
Did you like that?

69
00:04:51.912 --> 00:04:53.779
It was well struck.
Your Grace.

70
00:04:53.814 --> 00:04:56.149
I already said
it was well struck.

71
00:04:57.384 --> 00:04:59.519
Yes. Your Grace.

72
00:05:06.961 --> 00:05:09.096
- Who's next?
- Herald: <i>Lothor Brune.</i>

73
00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:12.600
freerider in the service
of Lord Baelish.

74
00:05:12.634 --> 00:05:16.070
Ser Dontos the Red
of House Hollard.

75
00:05:18.741 --> 00:05:21.576
Ser Dontos the Red
of House Hollard!

76
00:05:21.611 --> 00:05:23.145
Dontos:
<i>Here I am.</i>

77
00:05:23.179 --> 00:05:25.948
Here I am.

78
00:05:31.287 --> 00:05:33.888
Sorry. Your Grace.

79
00:05:33.922 --> 00:05:35.723
My deepest apologies.

80
00:05:35.757 --> 00:05:37.524
- Joffrey: <i>Are you drunk?</i>
- No.

81
00:05:37.559 --> 00:05:40.261
Uh. no.
No. Your Grace.

82
00:05:40.295 --> 00:05:43.063
- I had two cups of wine.
- Two cups?

83
00:05:43.097 --> 00:05:45.266
That's not much at all.

84
00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:47.768
Please.
have another cup.

85
00:05:47.803 --> 00:05:49.170
Are you sure. Your Grace?

86
00:05:49.205 --> 00:05:51.506
Joffrey: <i>Yes. To celebrate</i>
<i>my name day.</i>

87
00:05:51.541 --> 00:05:54.243
Have two.
Have as much as you like.

88
00:05:54.277 --> 00:05:57.214
I would be honored.
Your Grace.

89
00:05:58.616 --> 00:06:01.685
Ser Meryn. help Ser Dontos
celebrate my name day.

90
00:06:01.719 --> 00:06:04.020
See that he drinks
his fill.

91
00:06:07.157 --> 00:06:09.326
<i>( Crowd gasps )</i>

92
00:06:18.570 --> 00:06:21.538
( Gurgling )

93
00:06:21.572 --> 00:06:24.608
You can't.

94
00:06:24.642 --> 00:06:26.409
What did you say?

95
00:06:27.578 --> 00:06:29.445
Did you say I can't?

96
00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:32.148
I only meant
it would be bad luck

97
00:06:32.182 --> 00:06:33.916
to kill a man
on your name day.

98
00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:36.217
What kind of stupid
peasant's superstition...

99
00:06:36.252 --> 00:06:38.086
Hound:
<i>The girl is right.</i>

100
00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:39.887
<i>What a man sows</i>
<i>on his name day</i>

101
00:06:39.922 --> 00:06:41.456
he reaps all year.

102
00:06:41.490 --> 00:06:43.958
- <i>( Men laughing )</i>
- <i>( Wine pouring )</i>

103
00:06:43.993 --> 00:06:46.628
- <i>( Dontos gagging )</i>
- Take him away.

104
00:06:46.662 --> 00:06:48.897
I'll have him killed
tomorrow. the fool.

105
00:06:50.066 --> 00:06:51.800
<i>( Crowd murmuring )</i>

106
00:06:51.834 --> 00:06:53.435
He is.

107
00:06:53.469 --> 00:06:55.137
A fool--
you're so clever to see it.

108
00:06:55.171 --> 00:06:58.574
He'll make a much better fool
than a knight.

109
00:06:58.608 --> 00:07:01.911
He doesn't deserve
the mercy of a quick death.

110
00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:06.148
Did you hear My Lady.
Ser Dontos?

111
00:07:06.183 --> 00:07:09.319
From this day.
you'll be my new fool.

112
00:07:09.353 --> 00:07:11.521
Thank you. Your Grace.

113
00:07:11.556 --> 00:07:14.791
And you. My Lady.
thank you.

114
00:07:14.826 --> 00:07:17.795
Tyrion:
<i>Beloved nephew.</i>

115
00:07:24.002 --> 00:07:26.703
We looked for you
on the battlefield.

116
00:07:28.639 --> 00:07:32.041
You were nowhere
to be found.

117
00:07:32.075 --> 00:07:34.777
I've been here.
ruling the kingdoms.

118
00:07:34.811 --> 00:07:38.213
What a fine job
you've done.

119
00:07:38.247 --> 00:07:39.881
Look at you.

120
00:07:41.183 --> 00:07:43.318
More beautiful
than ever.

121
00:07:43.352 --> 00:07:47.522
And you! You-- you're going to be
bigger than the hound.

122
00:07:47.556 --> 00:07:50.024
- but much better looking.
- ( Laughs )

123
00:07:50.059 --> 00:07:51.960
This one doesn't like me.

124
00:07:51.994 --> 00:07:53.829
Can't imagine why.

125
00:07:53.863 --> 00:07:56.498
- We heard you were dead.
- I'm glad you're not dead.

126
00:07:56.533 --> 00:07:58.434
Me. too. dear.

127
00:07:58.468 --> 00:08:00.736
Death is so boring.
especially now

128
00:08:00.770 --> 00:08:03.773
with so much excitement
in the world.

129
00:08:03.807 --> 00:08:06.043
My Lady. I'm sorry
for your loss.

130
00:08:07.478 --> 00:08:09.113
Her loss?

131
00:08:09.147 --> 00:08:11.048
Her father was
a confessed traitor.

132
00:08:11.082 --> 00:08:12.683
But still her father.

133
00:08:12.718 --> 00:08:14.719
Surely having so recently
lost your own beloved father

134
00:08:14.753 --> 00:08:16.654
you can sympathize.

135
00:08:20.459 --> 00:08:22.593
My father was a traitor.

136
00:08:22.627 --> 00:08:24.494
My mother and brother
are traitors. too.

137
00:08:24.529 --> 00:08:27.731
I am loyal
to my beloved Joffrey.

138
00:08:28.933 --> 00:08:31.334
Of course you are.

139
00:08:32.970 --> 00:08:36.839
Well. enjoy your name day.
Your Grace.

140
00:08:36.874 --> 00:08:38.774
Wish I could stay
and celebrate.

141
00:08:38.809 --> 00:08:41.577
but there is work
to be done.

142
00:08:41.611 --> 00:08:43.612
What work?

143
00:08:43.647 --> 00:08:45.781
Why are you here?

144
00:08:48.651 --> 00:08:51.886
Pycelle: The raven arrived
from the Citadel

145
00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:55.056
- this morning. Your Grace.
-( Bird squawking )

146
00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:57.959
The conclave has met.
considered reports

147
00:08:57.993 --> 00:09:00.128
from Maesters all over
the Seven Kingdoms.

148
00:09:00.163 --> 00:09:03.598
<i>and declared</i>
<i>this great summer</i>

149
00:09:03.632 --> 00:09:06.434
done at last.

150
00:09:06.469 --> 00:09:09.271
The longest summer
in living memory.

151
00:09:09.305 --> 00:09:11.273
The peasants say.
a long summer means

152
00:09:11.307 --> 00:09:14.210
- <i>an even longer winter.</i>
- Pycelle: <i>A common superstition.</i>

153
00:09:14.244 --> 00:09:17.280
Littlefinger: <i>We have enough wheat</i>
<i>for a five-year winter.</i>

154
00:09:17.314 --> 00:09:19.582
If it lasts any longer.

155
00:09:19.616 --> 00:09:22.250
we'll have
fewer peasants.

156
00:09:22.285 --> 00:09:25.253
The city's drowning in refugees.
Your Grace. fleeing the war.

157
00:09:25.287 --> 00:09:26.754
We have nowhere
to house them.

158
00:09:26.788 --> 00:09:28.923
And with winter coming.
it'll only get worse.

159
00:09:28.957 --> 00:09:31.892
You command the City Watch.
do you not. Lord Slynt?

160
00:09:33.395 --> 00:09:35.262
<i>I do. Your Grace.</i>

161
00:09:35.297 --> 00:09:37.298
And are you not
a Lord at my command?

162
00:09:37.332 --> 00:09:40.835
I owe my title and lands
to your generosity. Your Grace.

163
00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:43.505
Then do your job.
Shut the gates to the peasants.

164
00:09:43.539 --> 00:09:46.474
They belong in the field.
not our capital.

165
00:09:46.509 --> 00:09:49.911
- Yes. Your Grace.
- <i>( Man whistling tune )</i>

166
00:09:54.616 --> 00:09:56.250
Don't get up.

167
00:09:57.419 --> 00:10:01.188
More ravishing than ever.
big sister.

168
00:10:02.257 --> 00:10:04.992
War agrees with you.

169
00:10:05.027 --> 00:10:07.928
Forgive the interruption.
Carry on.

170
00:10:09.163 --> 00:10:10.564
What are you doing here?

171
00:10:10.598 --> 00:10:14.300
Ah. it's been
a remarkable journey.

172
00:10:14.334 --> 00:10:18.004
I pissed off the edge
of the Wall.

173
00:10:18.038 --> 00:10:20.940
<i>I slept in a sky cell.</i>

174
00:10:20.974 --> 00:10:23.209
I fought with
the hill tribes--

175
00:10:23.244 --> 00:10:25.979
so many adventures.

176
00:10:26.013 --> 00:10:28.716
so much to be
thankful for.

177
00:10:28.750 --> 00:10:32.020
What are you doing here?
This is the small council.

178
00:10:32.782 --> 00:10:34.382
Yes. well I. do believe.
the Hand of the King.

179
00:10:35.425 --> 00:10:37.326
is welcome at all
small council meetings.

180
00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:39.362
Our father
is Hand of the King.

181
00:10:39.396 --> 00:10:42.432
Yes. but in his absence...

182
00:10:49.606 --> 00:10:51.841
Varys: <i>Your father has named</i>
<i>Lord Tyrion</i>

183
00:10:51.876 --> 00:10:54.611
to serve as Hand
in his stead while he fights.

184
00:10:54.645 --> 00:10:57.313
Out! All of you out!

185
00:11:01.986 --> 00:11:04.688
Cersei: I would like to know
how you tricked father into this.

186
00:11:04.722 --> 00:11:06.690
Tyrion: If I were capable
of tricking father.

187
00:11:06.724 --> 00:11:08.325
I'd be emperor
of the world by now.

188
00:11:08.359 --> 00:11:10.961
You brought this
on yourself.

189
00:11:10.995 --> 00:11:12.462
I've done nothing.

190
00:11:12.497 --> 00:11:14.364
Quite right--
you did nothing

191
00:11:14.399 --> 00:11:16.766
when your son called
for Ned Stark's head.

192
00:11:16.801 --> 00:11:18.768
Now the entire North
has risen up against us.

193
00:11:18.803 --> 00:11:21.271
- I tried to stop it.
- Did you? You failed.

194
00:11:21.305 --> 00:11:24.441
That bit of theater will haunt
our family for a generation.

195
00:11:24.475 --> 00:11:28.478
- Robb Stark is a child.
- Who's won every battle he's fought.

196
00:11:28.512 --> 00:11:30.714
Do you understand
we're losing the war?

197
00:11:30.748 --> 00:11:33.984
- What do you know about warfare?
- Nothing.

198
00:11:34.018 --> 00:11:35.786
But I know people.

199
00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:37.888
And I know that our enemies hate
each other

200
00:11:37.922 --> 00:11:40.824
almost as much
as they hate us.

201
00:11:45.130 --> 00:11:47.765
- Joffrey is King.
- Joffrey is King.

202
00:11:47.799 --> 00:11:50.334
You are here
to advise him.

203
00:11:50.368 --> 00:11:52.036
I'm only here
to advise him.

204
00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:54.605
And if the King listens
to what I say.

205
00:11:54.640 --> 00:11:58.275
the King might just get
his Uncle Jaime back.

206
00:11:59.978 --> 00:12:01.478
How?

207
00:12:01.513 --> 00:12:03.080
You love your children.

208
00:12:03.114 --> 00:12:04.614
It's your one
redeeming quality.

209
00:12:04.648 --> 00:12:07.583
That and your cheekbones.

210
00:12:07.618 --> 00:12:10.452
The Starks love
their children as well.

211
00:12:10.487 --> 00:12:13.088
- And we have two of them.
- One.

212
00:12:14.691 --> 00:12:17.659
- One?
- Arya. little animal-- she disappeared.

213
00:12:17.694 --> 00:12:20.729
Disappeared?
What. in a puff of smoke?

214
00:12:22.465 --> 00:12:25.801
We had three Starks
to trade.

215
00:12:25.835 --> 00:12:28.571
You chopped one's head off
and let another escape.

216
00:12:29.473 --> 00:12:31.573
Father will be furious.

217
00:12:32.642 --> 00:12:34.243
It must be odd for you...

218
00:12:36.747 --> 00:12:39.048
to be the disappointing child.

219
00:12:44.255 --> 00:12:46.523
<i>( Crow cawing )</i>

220
00:12:46.558 --> 00:12:50.394
Leadranach: <i>My Lord. may the Old Gods</i>
<i>watch over your brother</i>

221
00:12:50.429 --> 00:12:53.097
<i>and all our northern sons.</i>

222
00:12:53.132 --> 00:12:57.101
<i>The walls of my Holdfast</i>
<i>will not stand the winter.</i>

223
00:12:57.136 --> 00:13:01.005
The stones were last mortared
in the time of King Aerys.

224
00:13:01.039 --> 00:13:03.407
and I'm afraid
the masons today

225
00:13:03.441 --> 00:13:07.177
are not fit to carry
their fathers' hammers.

226
00:13:07.211 --> 00:13:09.612
When I was a boy.
I remember seeing them

227
00:13:09.647 --> 00:13:14.216
<i>put up a new tower</i>
<i>at Torrhen's Square in a summer.</i>

228
00:13:14.251 --> 00:13:16.352
<i>Men worked back then.</i>

229
00:13:16.386 --> 00:13:19.288
Today. my Holdfast
looks like it was built

230
00:13:19.323 --> 00:13:21.557
by drunk children.

231
00:13:21.592 --> 00:13:25.729
At night you can hear the wind
howling through the gaps.

232
00:13:25.763 --> 00:13:27.731
<i>And the Gods</i>
<i>forbid it rains.</i>

233
00:13:27.765 --> 00:13:31.001
Why. I might as well sleep
beneath a waterfall.

234
00:13:31.035 --> 00:13:32.670
Luwin:
<i>Maintenance of a Holdfast</i>

235
00:13:32.704 --> 00:13:36.107
generally falls
to the lord of that Holdfast.

236
00:13:36.142 --> 00:13:37.609
Generally. yes.

237
00:13:37.643 --> 00:13:39.310
but I've sent
all the young men off

238
00:13:39.344 --> 00:13:41.246
to fight
Robb Stark's war.

239
00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:44.382
King Robb.
And it's not his war.

240
00:13:44.416 --> 00:13:46.317
He didn't choose it.

241
00:13:46.351 --> 00:13:47.785
Maybe not. My Lord.

242
00:13:47.819 --> 00:13:49.920
but he called in his Banners
and took the men.

243
00:13:49.954 --> 00:13:51.688
Bran:
<i>Joffrey killed my father.</i>

244
00:13:51.722 --> 00:13:54.157
your liege lord.

245
00:13:54.191 --> 00:13:56.659
Do you remember
your vows. Ser?

246
00:13:56.693 --> 00:13:58.561
Of course I remember!

247
00:13:58.595 --> 00:14:01.664
We can spare four masons
for a week. My Lord.

248
00:14:01.698 --> 00:14:04.734
Will that be sufficient
to repair your walls?

249
00:14:04.768 --> 00:14:07.070
I-- I believe it will.

250
00:14:13.011 --> 00:14:15.380
We didn't want him here
all day. did we?

251
00:14:16.649 --> 00:14:19.684
I didn't like the way
he was talking about Robb.

252
00:14:19.719 --> 00:14:21.519
Nor did I.

253
00:14:23.789 --> 00:14:26.657
But listening to people
you'd rather not listen to

254
00:14:26.692 --> 00:14:30.762
is one of your responsibilities
as Lord of Winterfell.

255
00:14:30.796 --> 00:14:32.630
( Sighs )

256
00:14:33.665 --> 00:14:35.933
Luwin:
<i>Lord Portan.</i>

257
00:14:35.967 --> 00:14:39.002
<i>My Lord. may the Old Gods</i>
<i>watch over your brother</i>

258
00:14:39.036 --> 00:14:40.770
<i>and all our northern sons.</i>

259
00:14:40.805 --> 00:14:43.940
<i>( Heavy breathing )</i>

260
00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:53.616
- <i>( Wings flapping )</i>
- <i>( Bird squawking )</i>

261
00:15:29.722 --> 00:15:34.160
Boil this for an hour
and drink the tea.

262
00:15:34.194 --> 00:15:36.697
Makes all your pain
go away.

263
00:15:36.731 --> 00:15:39.366
Bran:
Don't have any pain.

264
00:15:39.400 --> 00:15:41.000
Lucky for you.

265
00:15:42.069 --> 00:15:43.903
That way.

266
00:15:46.640 --> 00:15:48.875
You've been having
those dreams again.

267
00:15:48.909 --> 00:15:50.743
Bran:
<i>I don't dream.</i>

268
00:15:50.777 --> 00:15:52.311
Everyone dreams.

269
00:15:52.345 --> 00:15:55.280
I don't.

270
00:15:55.314 --> 00:15:57.382
Heard some of the men
talking about the comet.

271
00:15:57.416 --> 00:15:59.551
<i>They say it's an omen.</i>

272
00:15:59.585 --> 00:16:03.255
They say it means Robb will win
a great victory in the South.

273
00:16:03.289 --> 00:16:04.890
Did they?

274
00:16:06.659 --> 00:16:10.229
Osha: I heard some other fools
say it's Lannister Red.

275
00:16:10.264 --> 00:16:13.633
Means the Lannisters will rule
all Seven Kingdoms before long.

276
00:16:13.667 --> 00:16:17.070
Heard a stableboy say
it's the color of blood

277
00:16:17.104 --> 00:16:19.473
to mark the death
of your father.

278
00:16:23.311 --> 00:16:26.546
The stars
don't fall for men.

279
00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:29.148
The red comet means
one thing. boy--

280
00:16:30.283 --> 00:16:31.884
dragons.

281
00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:36.454
The dragons are all dead.

282
00:16:36.489 --> 00:16:38.957
They've been dead
for centuries.

283
00:17:11.825 --> 00:17:14.226
( Shrieks )

284
00:17:15.495 --> 00:17:17.263
Mmm.

285
00:17:17.297 --> 00:17:20.232
Mmm. Mmm.

286
00:17:22.335 --> 00:17:24.970
What did your brother say
about them. Khaleesi?

287
00:17:25.004 --> 00:17:26.672
He said they ate meat.

288
00:17:26.707 --> 00:17:30.409
He didn't tell you
what kind of meat?

289
00:17:30.443 --> 00:17:33.345
My brother didn't know
anything about dragons.

290
00:17:33.379 --> 00:17:36.514
He didn't know anything
about anything.

291
00:17:41.454 --> 00:17:43.989
Eh.

292
00:17:45.725 --> 00:17:48.861
( Whinnies )

293
00:17:50.030 --> 00:17:52.532
<i>( Women murmuring )</i>

294
00:18:10.318 --> 00:18:12.386
She was Drogo's
first gift to me.

295
00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:15.422
I remember.

296
00:18:17.291 --> 00:18:19.927
I promised
to protect them.

297
00:18:19.961 --> 00:18:22.295
Promised them their enemies
would die screaming.

298
00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:24.831
How do I make
starvation scream?

299
00:18:24.866 --> 00:18:27.868
A trick I never learned.
I'm afraid.

300
00:18:29.704 --> 00:18:31.771
Does it ever end?

301
00:18:31.806 --> 00:18:33.773
This is farther east
than I've ever been.

302
00:18:33.807 --> 00:18:35.341
But. yes. Khaleesi.

303
00:18:35.376 --> 00:18:36.843
everything ends.
even the red waste.

304
00:18:36.877 --> 00:18:39.445
And you're sure
there's no other way?

305
00:18:39.480 --> 00:18:42.215
If we go south to the land
of the Lazarheen.

306
00:18:42.249 --> 00:18:44.717
the Lamb Men will kill us
and take your dragons.

307
00:18:44.752 --> 00:18:46.652
If we go west
to the Dothraki Sea.

308
00:18:46.687 --> 00:18:48.721
the first
Khalasar we meet

309
00:18:48.755 --> 00:18:50.289
will kill us
and take your dragons.

310
00:18:50.323 --> 00:18:52.992
No one will take
my dragons.

311
00:18:54.161 --> 00:18:56.863
They are too weak to fight.

312
00:18:56.897 --> 00:18:58.898
as are your people.

313
00:18:58.932 --> 00:19:01.268
You must be
their strength.

314
00:19:02.203 --> 00:19:04.338
As you are mine.

315
00:19:07.842 --> 00:19:10.478
( Speaks Dothraki )

316
00:19:16.219 --> 00:19:18.787
( Speaking Dothraki )

317
00:19:40.641 --> 00:19:43.009
( Speaks Dothraki )

318
00:19:51.318 --> 00:19:54.254
Rakharo...

319
00:20:00.762 --> 00:20:03.531
You never have.

320
00:20:08.369 --> 00:20:12.205
This is bad time to start.

321
00:20:25.153 --> 00:20:27.955
<i>( Horse whinnies )</i>

322
00:20:51.513 --> 00:20:54.548
<i>( Wind howling )</i>

323
00:20:56.151 --> 00:20:58.319
<i>( Thunder rumbling )</i>

324
00:21:06.628 --> 00:21:08.262
<i>( Bird caws )</i>

325
00:21:08.297 --> 00:21:10.265
Having a rough time of it?

326
00:21:10.299 --> 00:21:11.866
Nothing's killed me yet.

327
00:21:11.901 --> 00:21:14.469
- Grenn: Your ass killed the sledge.
- You offered me a ride.

328
00:21:14.504 --> 00:21:17.739
I just wanted you to shut up about
your damn blisters.

329
00:21:31.753 --> 00:21:34.555
I was born in a place
like this.

330
00:21:34.590 --> 00:21:37.725
Later. I fell
on hard times.

331
00:21:39.361 --> 00:21:41.128
Samwell:
<i>Are those girls?</i>

332
00:21:41.162 --> 00:21:42.963
Dolorous Edd:
<i>Craster's daughters.</i>

333
00:21:42.998 --> 00:21:46.734
I haven't seen a girl
in six months.

334
00:21:46.768 --> 00:21:48.703
I'd keep on not seeing them
if I were you.

335
00:21:48.737 --> 00:21:52.139
What. he don't like people messing
with his daughters?

336
00:21:52.174 --> 00:21:54.976
He don't like people
messing with his wives.

337
00:21:56.345 --> 00:21:58.579
He marries
his daughters.

338
00:21:58.614 --> 00:22:00.949
<i>and they give him</i>
<i>more daughters.</i>

339
00:22:00.983 --> 00:22:03.184
And on and on it goes.

340
00:22:03.219 --> 00:22:05.653
- That's foul.
- It's beyond foul.

341
00:22:05.687 --> 00:22:09.591
All the other wildlings for a
hundred leagues have disappeared.

342
00:22:09.625 --> 00:22:11.592
Craster's still here.

343
00:22:11.627 --> 00:22:14.262
He must be doing
something right.

344
00:22:15.898 --> 00:22:17.599
What happens
to the boys?

345
00:22:17.633 --> 00:22:20.668
- Hmm?
- <i>He marries his daughters.</i>

346
00:22:20.703 --> 00:22:23.605
What does he do
with his sons?

347
00:22:25.942 --> 00:22:28.643
He said he planned
to stop here

348
00:22:28.678 --> 00:22:30.245
on his way
to the Frostfangs.

349
00:22:30.279 --> 00:22:31.880
People make
all sorts of plans.

350
00:22:31.914 --> 00:22:35.350
I haven't seen Benjen Stark
in three years.

351
00:22:35.384 --> 00:22:36.851
Haven't missed him.

352
00:22:36.886 --> 00:22:39.621
Always treated me
like scum.

353
00:22:40.890 --> 00:22:43.525
Haven't had any good wine
for a long time.

354
00:22:43.559 --> 00:22:46.561
You Southerners make good wine.
I'll give you that.

355
00:22:46.595 --> 00:22:48.630
We're not Southerners.

356
00:22:48.665 --> 00:22:50.399
Who's this little girl?

357
00:22:51.868 --> 00:22:54.670
You're prettier
than half my daughters.

358
00:22:54.705 --> 00:22:58.040
You got a nice wet twat
between your legs?

359
00:22:58.074 --> 00:22:59.808
What's your name?

360
00:22:59.843 --> 00:23:01.843
- Jon Snow.
- Snow. eh?

361
00:23:01.878 --> 00:23:04.712
Listen to me. bastard.

362
00:23:04.747 --> 00:23:08.716
All you lot from south of the Wall.
you're Southerners.

363
00:23:08.750 --> 00:23:12.620
But now you're in the North.
the real North.

364
00:23:12.654 --> 00:23:14.254
The lad meant no harm.

365
00:23:15.757 --> 00:23:18.992
I catch that pretty little bastard
talking to my daughters--

366
00:23:19.027 --> 00:23:23.164
No one will talk to your daughters.
you have my word.

367
00:23:23.198 --> 00:23:26.535
Now. sit down
and shut your mouth.

368
00:23:29.239 --> 00:23:31.541
You bring any of that
good wine with you?

369
00:23:31.575 --> 00:23:33.410
We did.

370
00:23:33.444 --> 00:23:35.946
We passed through
six villages on the way here.

371
00:23:35.980 --> 00:23:37.814
All six were abandoned.

372
00:23:37.849 --> 00:23:40.917
Where have all
the wildlings gone?

373
00:23:40.951 --> 00:23:44.487
I could tell you.
but I'm thirsty.

374
00:23:44.521 --> 00:23:46.623
Mormont: <i>There's a barrel of</i>
<i>Dornish wine on the sledge.</i>

375
00:23:46.657 --> 00:23:49.392
- <i>Bring it in here.</i>
- Man: <i>Yes. commander.</i>

376
00:23:49.426 --> 00:23:52.595
Craster: <i>You want to know</i>
<i>where they've all gone?</i>

377
00:23:52.629 --> 00:23:56.932
<i>North... to join up</i>
<i>with Mance Rayder...</i>

378
00:23:58.101 --> 00:23:59.834
Your old friend.

379
00:23:59.869 --> 00:24:02.504
He's no friend of mine.

380
00:24:02.539 --> 00:24:05.671
He broke his vows.
betrayed his brothers.

381
00:24:05.696 --> 00:24:06.896
Oh. aye.

382
00:24:07.010 --> 00:24:10.080
But once he was
just a poor black crow.

383
00:24:10.114 --> 00:24:13.050
And now he's
King-Beyond-the-Wall.

384
00:24:13.085 --> 00:24:15.553
He's been calling
himself that for years.

385
00:24:15.587 --> 00:24:19.324
What's he king of?
A frozen lake somewhere?

386
00:24:20.693 --> 00:24:22.761
That's a good-looking axe.

387
00:24:22.795 --> 00:24:24.930
<i>Fresh forged?</i>

388
00:24:26.933 --> 00:24:29.468
Give it here.

389
00:24:29.502 --> 00:24:31.670
You'll have another one
made at Castle Black.

390
00:24:31.705 --> 00:24:33.606
Here.

391
00:24:33.640 --> 00:24:37.443
Oh. that's some
lovely steel.

392
00:24:41.147 --> 00:24:44.283
You want to know
what Mance Rayder is doing?

393
00:24:44.317 --> 00:24:46.118
Gathering an army.

394
00:24:46.186 --> 00:24:48.387
<i>What I hear.</i>
<i>he's already got more men</i>

395
00:24:48.421 --> 00:24:50.723
<i>than any of your</i>
<i>southern kings.</i>

396
00:24:50.757 --> 00:24:53.259
And where does he plan
marching this army?

397
00:24:53.293 --> 00:24:54.760
When you're
all the way north.

398
00:24:54.794 --> 00:24:56.529
there's only
one direction to go.

399
00:24:58.732 --> 00:25:03.369
These are bad times to be
living alone in the wild.

400
00:25:03.404 --> 00:25:06.706
The cold winds
are rising.

401
00:25:06.741 --> 00:25:10.243
Let them come.
My roots are sunk deep.

402
00:25:11.746 --> 00:25:13.746
Wife...

403
00:25:13.781 --> 00:25:17.817
tell the Lord Crow
how content we are.

404
00:25:17.851 --> 00:25:20.219
This is our place.

405
00:25:20.253 --> 00:25:22.154
Our husband keeps us safe.

406
00:25:22.189 --> 00:25:25.358
Better to live free
than die a slave.

407
00:25:27.127 --> 00:25:30.630
Craster: <i>Don't it make you</i>
<i>jealous. old man.</i>

408
00:25:30.664 --> 00:25:32.732
to see me with
all these young wives

409
00:25:32.766 --> 00:25:36.035
and you with no one
to warm your bed?

410
00:25:36.069 --> 00:25:38.004
We chose different paths.

411
00:25:38.038 --> 00:25:42.475
Oh. aye. and you chose the path
with no one but boys on it.

412
00:25:44.344 --> 00:25:47.479
You'll be wanting to sleep
beneath my roof. I suppose.

413
00:25:47.514 --> 00:25:49.581
and eat me out of pigs.

414
00:25:49.616 --> 00:25:51.517
A roof would be welcome.

415
00:25:51.551 --> 00:25:53.085
It's been hard riding.

416
00:25:53.119 --> 00:25:56.321
We've brought our own food
and good steel for you.

417
00:25:58.925 --> 00:26:01.660
Any man lays a hand
on one of my wives.

418
00:26:01.694 --> 00:26:04.663
he loses the hand.

419
00:26:06.499 --> 00:26:10.301
And I see this one
staring too long.

420
00:26:10.336 --> 00:26:13.571
I might just gouge
his eyes out.

421
00:26:13.605 --> 00:26:16.875
Your roof. your rules.

422
00:26:28.389 --> 00:26:29.822
( Grunts )

423
00:26:29.857 --> 00:26:32.158
Who am I?!

424
00:26:32.193 --> 00:26:35.629
- Who am I?!
- Lord commander.

425
00:26:35.663 --> 00:26:38.832
- And who are you?
- Jon Snow.

426
00:26:38.866 --> 00:26:41.468
Who <i>are</i> you?

427
00:26:41.502 --> 00:26:43.770
Your steward.

428
00:26:43.804 --> 00:26:45.905
You want to lead
one day?

429
00:26:48.675 --> 00:26:51.410
Then learn
how to follow.

430
00:27:02.788 --> 00:27:05.958
<i>( Man panting )</i>

431
00:27:08.929 --> 00:27:13.666
Melisandre: <i>Lord of Light. come to us</i>
<i>in our darkness.</i>

432
00:27:13.700 --> 00:27:17.404
We offer you
these false Gods.

433
00:27:17.438 --> 00:27:20.373
Take them and cast
your light upon us...

434
00:27:22.076 --> 00:27:26.112
For the night is dark
and full of terrors.

435
00:27:26.146 --> 00:27:29.648
Men: For the night is dark
and full of terrors.

436
00:27:31.617 --> 00:27:33.551
Melisandre:
<i>After the long summer.</i>

437
00:27:33.585 --> 00:27:36.621
<i>darkness will fall heavy</i>
<i>on the world.</i>

438
00:27:36.655 --> 00:27:39.357
The stars will bleed.

439
00:27:39.391 --> 00:27:41.760
We need to stop her.

440
00:27:41.794 --> 00:27:45.597
Melisandre: <i>The cold breath of winter</i>
<i>will freeze the seas...</i>

441
00:27:45.631 --> 00:27:47.029
Not now.

442
00:27:47.054 --> 00:27:48.254
<i>...And the dead shall rise</i>
<i>in the North.</i>

443
00:27:51.804 --> 00:27:55.374
All you men were named
in the Light of the Seven!

444
00:27:55.409 --> 00:27:58.544
<i>Is this how you treat</i>
<i>the Gods of your fathers?</i>

445
00:27:58.579 --> 00:28:03.282
Are you so eager to spit
on your ancestors?

446
00:28:11.857 --> 00:28:14.291
You smell of fear--

447
00:28:14.359 --> 00:28:18.595
fear and piss
and old bones.

448
00:28:19.830 --> 00:28:21.531
Do you want to stop me?

449
00:28:25.970 --> 00:28:27.837
Stop me.

450
00:28:40.652 --> 00:28:42.386
In the ancient books.
it's written

451
00:28:42.421 --> 00:28:46.457
that a warrior will draw
a burning sword from the fire.

452
00:28:47.593 --> 00:28:50.661
And that sword shall be
Lightbringer.

453
00:28:55.468 --> 00:28:58.970
Stannis Baratheon.

454
00:28:59.004 --> 00:29:01.572
warrior of light.

455
00:29:01.607 --> 00:29:03.508
your sword awaits you.

456
00:29:24.764 --> 00:29:27.032
<i>( Men cheering )</i>

457
00:29:33.774 --> 00:29:37.243
Men: Lord. cast your
light upon us!

458
00:29:38.778 --> 00:29:42.114
Melisandre: <i>For the night is dark</i>
<i>and full of terrors.</i>

459
00:29:44.951 --> 00:29:48.420
For the night is dark
and full of terror.

460
00:30:15.482 --> 00:30:19.117
This woman will lead him
into a war he cannot win.

461
00:30:19.152 --> 00:30:20.785
Stannis is our king.

462
00:30:20.820 --> 00:30:22.153
We follow
where he leads.

463
00:30:22.188 --> 00:30:24.889
- even if we don't like the path.
- King.

464
00:30:24.923 --> 00:30:27.024
Since that boar
killed his brother.

465
00:30:27.059 --> 00:30:29.093
every lord wants
a coronation.

466
00:30:29.127 --> 00:30:31.228
I don't serve the others.
I serve Stannis.

467
00:30:31.263 --> 00:30:34.965
As do I.
but loyal service

468
00:30:34.999 --> 00:30:37.935
means telling
hard truths.

469
00:30:37.969 --> 00:30:42.038
He's surrounded
by fools and fanatics.

470
00:30:42.073 --> 00:30:44.841
but he trusts you. Davos.

471
00:30:44.876 --> 00:30:47.978
If you tell him
the truth...

472
00:30:49.381 --> 00:30:51.316
What's the truth?

473
00:31:03.963 --> 00:31:05.764
Matthos: <i>"And I declare upon</i>
<i>the honor of my house</i>

474
00:31:05.798 --> 00:31:07.232
<i>that my beloved</i>
<i>brother Robert--"</i>

475
00:31:07.266 --> 00:31:09.868
he wasn't
my beloved brother.

476
00:31:09.902 --> 00:31:12.103
I didn't love him.
He didn't love me.

477
00:31:12.138 --> 00:31:13.972
A harmless courtesy.
Your Grace.

478
00:31:14.006 --> 00:31:15.373
A lie.
Take it out.

479
00:31:18.310 --> 00:31:20.211
"...that my brother Robert
left no trueborn heirs.

480
00:31:20.245 --> 00:31:22.647
the boy Joffrey.
the boy Tommen.

481
00:31:22.681 --> 00:31:24.849
and the girl Myrcella
being born of incest

482
00:31:24.884 --> 00:31:27.887
<i>between Cersei Lannister and</i>
<i>her brother Jaime Lannister.</i>

483
00:31:27.921 --> 00:31:30.823
- <i>By right of birth--"</i>
- Jaime Lannister. the Kingslayer.

484
00:31:30.857 --> 00:31:33.659
Call him what he is.

485
00:31:33.694 --> 00:31:35.194
Matthos: <i>"...And her brother</i>
<i>Jaime Lannister.</i>

486
00:31:35.229 --> 00:31:36.596
<i>the Kingslayer.</i>

487
00:31:36.631 --> 00:31:39.867
<i>By right of birth and blood.</i>
<i>i do this day lay claim--"</i>

488
00:31:39.901 --> 00:31:43.036
Stannis: <i>Make it</i> Ser <i>Jaime Lannister.</i>
<i>the Kingslayer.</i>

489
00:31:43.071 --> 00:31:45.272
Whatever else he is.
the man's still a knight.

490
00:31:45.307 --> 00:31:47.341
"Ser Jaime Lannister.
the Kingslayer.

491
00:31:47.375 --> 00:31:49.710
By right of birth
and blood.

492
00:31:49.744 --> 00:31:53.181
<i>I do this day lay claim</i>
<i>to the Iron Throne of Westeros.</i>

493
00:31:53.215 --> 00:31:55.716
Let all true men
declare their loyalty."

494
00:31:55.751 --> 00:31:58.085
When Eddard Stark learned
the truth. he told only me.

495
00:31:58.120 --> 00:32:00.521
I'll not make
the same mistake.

496
00:32:00.555 --> 00:32:02.590
Send copies of that letter
to every corner of the Realm.

497
00:32:02.624 --> 00:32:04.491
from the Arbor
to the Wall.

498
00:32:04.526 --> 00:32:07.428
The time has come
to choose.

499
00:32:07.462 --> 00:32:09.930
Let no man claim ignorance
as an excuse.

500
00:32:09.965 --> 00:32:12.566
Your Grace.the Lannisters
are the true enemy.

501
00:32:12.601 --> 00:32:14.635
If. for the time being. you could
make peace with your brother--

502
00:32:14.669 --> 00:32:16.937
I'll not make peace with Renly
while he calls himself King.

503
00:32:16.972 --> 00:32:18.806
Well. many have already
declared for him--

504
00:32:18.840 --> 00:32:20.975
Mace Tyrell.
Randyll Tarly.

505
00:32:21.010 --> 00:32:24.245
Stannis does not need to beg
this lord or that lord for support.

506
00:32:24.279 --> 00:32:25.847
<i>The Lord of Light</i>
<i>stands behind him.</i>

507
00:32:25.881 --> 00:32:29.350
And how many ships has
the Lord of Light got in his fleet?

508
00:32:29.385 --> 00:32:31.953
- He has no need for ships.
- I'm sure he doesn't.

509
00:32:31.987 --> 00:32:33.388
but we do if we're
going to war.

510
00:32:33.422 --> 00:32:36.491
If not Renly. Your Grace.
join forces with Robb Stark.

511
00:32:36.525 --> 00:32:38.827
Who would steal
the northern half of my kingdom.

512
00:32:38.861 --> 00:32:40.162
I've always served thieves
according to their desserts.

513
00:32:40.196 --> 00:32:42.331
<i>as you well know.</i>
<i>Ser Davos.</i>

514
00:32:42.365 --> 00:32:45.366
Joffrey. Renly. Robb Stark.
they're all thieves.

515
00:32:45.401 --> 00:32:47.869
They'll bend the knee
or I'll destroy them.

516
00:32:47.903 --> 00:32:52.473
I owe you
an apology. my King.

517
00:32:52.508 --> 00:32:54.576
My duty is to serve.

518
00:32:54.610 --> 00:32:58.679
<i>You have chosen the new God</i>
<i>over the Old Gods.</i>

519
00:32:58.714 --> 00:33:02.216
<i>May the Lord of Light</i>
<i>watch over us all.</i>

520
00:33:02.251 --> 00:33:04.618
Shall we drink together?

521
00:33:04.653 --> 00:33:06.654
Don't.

522
00:33:06.688 --> 00:33:11.493
A cup of wine to honor
the one true God.

523
00:33:53.672 --> 00:33:55.140
( Thuds )

524
00:33:55.174 --> 00:33:57.576
( Men murmuring )

525
00:33:57.610 --> 00:34:00.812
The night is dark and full
of terrors. old man.

526
00:34:00.847 --> 00:34:04.082
but the fire
burns them all away.

527
00:34:08.788 --> 00:34:12.123
( Chatter )

528
00:34:25.638 --> 00:34:27.639
Man:
Your Grace.

529
00:34:39.019 --> 00:34:41.688
King in the North.

530
00:34:43.624 --> 00:34:45.425
I keep expecting you
to leave me

531
00:34:45.460 --> 00:34:47.494
in one castle or another
for safekeeping.

532
00:34:47.529 --> 00:34:51.565
but you drag me along
from camp to camp.

533
00:34:51.599 --> 00:34:54.234
Have you grown
fond of me. Stark?

534
00:34:54.269 --> 00:34:56.069
Is that it?

535
00:34:56.104 --> 00:34:58.105
I've never seen you
with a girl.

536
00:34:59.207 --> 00:35:01.642
If I left you with
one of my bannermen.

537
00:35:01.676 --> 00:35:04.712
your father would know
within a fortnight

538
00:35:04.746 --> 00:35:08.216
and my bannerman would receive
a raven with a message:

539
00:35:08.250 --> 00:35:11.819
"Release my son and you'll be rich
beyond your dreams.

540
00:35:11.854 --> 00:35:15.390
Refuse and your house
will be destroyed. root and stem."

541
00:35:15.424 --> 00:35:17.725
You don't trust
the loyalty

542
00:35:17.760 --> 00:35:20.061
of the men following
you into battle?

543
00:35:20.096 --> 00:35:23.599
Oh. I trust them
with my life.

544
00:35:23.633 --> 00:35:25.634
just not with yours.

545
00:35:25.668 --> 00:35:27.502
Smart boy.

546
00:35:27.537 --> 00:35:29.171
What's wrong?

547
00:35:29.205 --> 00:35:31.172
<i>Don't like</i>
<i>being called "boy"?</i>

548
00:35:32.107 --> 00:35:34.142
Insulted?

549
00:35:36.345 --> 00:35:38.646
<i>( Direwolf snarling )</i>

550
00:35:41.116 --> 00:35:43.984
Robb: <i>You insult yourself.</i>
<i>Kingslayer.</i>

551
00:35:45.653 --> 00:35:49.055
- <i>You've been defeated by a boy.</i>
- <i>( Heavy breathing )</i>

552
00:35:49.090 --> 00:35:51.557
<i>You're held captive</i>
<i>by a boy.</i>

553
00:35:53.660 --> 00:35:56.262
<i>Perhaps you'll be</i>
<i>killed by a boy.</i>

554
00:36:03.003 --> 00:36:04.771
Stannis Baratheon
sent ravens

555
00:36:04.806 --> 00:36:08.175
to all the high lords
of Westeros.

556
00:36:08.210 --> 00:36:11.880
King Joffrey Baratheon
is neither a true king

557
00:36:11.914 --> 00:36:14.549
<i>nor a true Baratheon.</i>

558
00:36:14.584 --> 00:36:16.718
He's your bastard son.

559
00:36:16.753 --> 00:36:19.322
<i>If that's true.</i>
<i>Stannis is the rightful king.</i>

560
00:36:19.356 --> 00:36:21.390
How convenient for him.

561
00:36:21.424 --> 00:36:25.694
My father learned
the truth.

562
00:36:25.729 --> 00:36:27.396
That's why
you had him executed.

563
00:36:27.431 --> 00:36:29.799
I was your prisoner
when Ned Stark lost his head.

564
00:36:29.833 --> 00:36:31.935
Your son killed him

565
00:36:31.969 --> 00:36:33.403
so the world wouldn't
learn who fathered him.

566
00:36:33.437 --> 00:36:37.474
And you-- you pushed
my brother from a window

567
00:36:37.508 --> 00:36:39.476
because he saw you
with the queen.

568
00:36:41.146 --> 00:36:43.047
( Snarling )

569
00:36:44.649 --> 00:36:47.685
You have proof?

570
00:36:47.719 --> 00:36:50.221
Or do you want to trade gossip
like a couple of fishwives?

571
00:36:50.256 --> 00:36:52.424
I'm sending one of your cousins
down to King's Landing

572
00:36:52.459 --> 00:36:54.093
with my peace terms.

573
00:36:54.127 --> 00:36:57.163
You think my father's going
to negotiate with you?

574
00:36:57.197 --> 00:36:59.599
You don't know him
very well.

575
00:36:59.633 --> 00:37:04.003
No. but he's starting
to know me.

576
00:37:04.037 --> 00:37:07.672
<i>Three victories</i>
<i>don't make you a conqueror.</i>

577
00:37:09.141 --> 00:37:11.776
It's better than
three defeats.

578
00:37:16.181 --> 00:37:19.650
( Snarling )

579
00:37:40.208 --> 00:37:42.809
Shae:
<i>This city stinks...</i>

580
00:37:42.843 --> 00:37:45.178
( Sniffs )

581
00:37:45.213 --> 00:37:46.780
Like dead bodies.

582
00:37:46.814 --> 00:37:48.948
Tyrion:
<i>A bit corpsey. yes.</i>

583
00:37:48.982 --> 00:37:51.450
And shit.

584
00:37:51.485 --> 00:37:53.385
I thought you wanted
to come here.

585
00:37:56.722 --> 00:37:59.090
I love it.

586
00:37:59.124 --> 00:38:02.794
You love the smell
of dead bodies and shit?

587
00:38:02.828 --> 00:38:05.864
And cum and garlic
and rum.

588
00:38:05.898 --> 00:38:09.034
You can smell cum
from the balcony?

589
00:38:09.068 --> 00:38:12.405
I love the stink.
I love the noise.

590
00:38:12.439 --> 00:38:14.541
Cities make me
want to fuck.

591
00:38:14.575 --> 00:38:17.878
And so did the country.

592
00:38:19.114 --> 00:38:20.948
( Sighs )

593
00:38:20.982 --> 00:38:22.482
This is where I belong.

594
00:38:22.517 --> 00:38:25.385
Yes. well. you need
to be careful.

595
00:38:25.419 --> 00:38:26.986
No one can know
you're here.

596
00:38:27.021 --> 00:38:28.688
No one will know.

597
00:38:28.722 --> 00:38:30.289
You can't trust anyone
in King's Landing.

598
00:38:30.324 --> 00:38:33.492
<i>They're all liars--</i>
<i>good liars. bad liars.</i>

599
00:38:33.527 --> 00:38:35.961
one or two great liars.

600
00:38:35.995 --> 00:38:37.996
What about you?

601
00:38:38.030 --> 00:38:40.665
Me? I'm not from here.
I'm a slave to the truth.

602
00:38:40.699 --> 00:38:43.501
( Laughs )
Truth?

603
00:38:43.535 --> 00:38:45.269
( Laughs )

604
00:38:45.304 --> 00:38:48.473
You are the biggest
little liar I have ever met.

605
00:38:48.507 --> 00:38:50.508
Why do you think
I am so little?

606
00:38:50.542 --> 00:38:55.078
I'm being crushed beneath the
weight of all that truth.

607
00:38:57.248 --> 00:38:59.215
Oh!

608
00:38:59.250 --> 00:39:02.052
Ned Stark actually
slept on this.

609
00:39:02.086 --> 00:39:05.923
As if the poor man
didn't suffer enough.

610
00:39:07.726 --> 00:39:11.196
One of the many changes
we'll have to make around here.

611
00:39:22.374 --> 00:39:25.676
- Lord Baelish.
- Your Grace.

612
00:39:25.711 --> 00:39:28.279
I wonder if I might
ask you for a favor.

613
00:39:28.313 --> 00:39:29.814
Of course.
Your Grace.

614
00:39:29.848 --> 00:39:31.782
Ned Stark's youngest
daughter Arya--

615
00:39:31.817 --> 00:39:34.018
we can't seem
to locate her.

616
00:39:34.052 --> 00:39:36.553
If she's escaped
the capital.

617
00:39:36.588 --> 00:39:38.655
Winterfell seems
the logical destination.

618
00:39:38.689 --> 00:39:41.225
And yet my friends in the North
report no sign of her.

619
00:39:41.259 --> 00:39:43.193
Curious.

620
00:39:43.228 --> 00:39:45.362
If we choose to negotiate
with the Starks.

621
00:39:45.397 --> 00:39:47.665
the girl has some value.
Whoever finds her--

622
00:39:47.699 --> 00:39:50.234
well. you know what they say about
Lannisters and debts.

623
00:39:50.269 --> 00:39:52.270
Well. you could ask
Varys where she is.

624
00:39:52.305 --> 00:39:54.606
He'll have
an answer for you.

625
00:39:54.641 --> 00:39:56.208
Whether you believe it...

626
00:39:56.242 --> 00:40:00.113
Myself. I have always had
a hard time trusting eunuchs.

627
00:40:00.147 --> 00:40:02.782
- Who knows what they want?
- ( Chuckles )

628
00:40:02.816 --> 00:40:05.918
A mockingbird.

629
00:40:05.953 --> 00:40:07.712
You created your
own Sigil. didn't you?

630
00:40:07.737 --> 00:40:08.937
Yes.

631
00:40:09.489 --> 00:40:11.791
Appropriate...
for a self-made man

632
00:40:11.825 --> 00:40:13.559
with so many
songs to sing.

633
00:40:13.593 --> 00:40:15.227
I'm glad you like it.

634
00:40:15.262 --> 00:40:17.130
Some people are
fortunate enough

635
00:40:17.164 --> 00:40:18.797
to be born into
the right family.

636
00:40:18.832 --> 00:40:21.500
Others have to find
their own way.

637
00:40:22.869 --> 00:40:24.903
I heard a song once

638
00:40:24.937 --> 00:40:27.572
about a boy
of modest means

639
00:40:27.606 --> 00:40:31.342
who found his way into the
home of a very prominent family.

640
00:40:31.376 --> 00:40:33.144
He loved
the eldest daughter.

641
00:40:33.178 --> 00:40:36.581
Sadly. she had eyes
for another.

642
00:40:36.615 --> 00:40:38.983
When boys and girls
live in the same home.

643
00:40:39.017 --> 00:40:41.652
awkward situations
can arise.

644
00:40:41.686 --> 00:40:44.321
Sometimes. I've heard.
even brothers and sisters

645
00:40:44.355 --> 00:40:46.856
develop
certain affections.

646
00:40:46.891 --> 00:40:49.325
And when these affections
become common knowledge.

647
00:40:49.359 --> 00:40:53.228
well. that is an awkward
situation indeed.

648
00:40:53.263 --> 00:40:55.564
especially
in a prominent family.

649
00:40:55.598 --> 00:40:59.034
But prominent families
often forget a simple truth.

650
00:40:59.068 --> 00:41:01.303
I've found.

651
00:41:01.337 --> 00:41:03.472
And which truth is that?

652
00:41:03.506 --> 00:41:07.143
Knowledge is power.

653
00:41:09.313 --> 00:41:11.715
Seize him.

654
00:41:13.551 --> 00:41:15.553
Cut his throat.

655
00:41:16.688 --> 00:41:19.157
Stop. Wait.

656
00:41:19.191 --> 00:41:21.560
I've changed my mind.
Let him go.

657
00:41:24.497 --> 00:41:26.197
Step back three paces.

658
00:41:27.600 --> 00:41:30.001
Turn around.

659
00:41:30.035 --> 00:41:31.702
Close your eyes.

660
00:41:35.908 --> 00:41:38.343
Power is power.

661
00:41:40.078 --> 00:41:41.565
Do see if you can
take some time away from

662
00:41:41.590 --> 00:41:43.504
your coins and your whores

663
00:41:43.849 --> 00:41:45.650
to locate
the Stark girl for me.

664
00:41:45.684 --> 00:41:49.220
I would very much
appreciate it.

665
00:41:59.031 --> 00:42:01.232
Robb:
<i>You're Ser Alton Lannister?</i>

666
00:42:01.266 --> 00:42:03.835
I am. Your Grace.

667
00:42:03.869 --> 00:42:07.406
<i>I offer your cousins peace</i>
<i>if they meet my terms.</i>

668
00:42:07.440 --> 00:42:11.743
First. your family
must release my sisters.

669
00:42:11.778 --> 00:42:15.446
Second. my father's bones
must be returned to us

670
00:42:15.480 --> 00:42:17.414
so he may rest beside
his brother and sister

671
00:42:17.449 --> 00:42:20.184
in the crypts
beneath Winterfell.

672
00:42:20.218 --> 00:42:22.387
And the remains of all those
who died in his service

673
00:42:22.421 --> 00:42:24.622
must also be returned.

674
00:42:24.657 --> 00:42:27.159
Their families can honor
them with proper funerals.

675
00:42:27.194 --> 00:42:30.262
- An honorable request. Your Grace.
- <i>Third...</i>

676
00:42:31.932 --> 00:42:34.401
Joffrey and the Queen Regent
must renounce all claim

677
00:42:34.435 --> 00:42:37.037
to dominion of the North.

678
00:42:37.072 --> 00:42:39.273
From this time
till the end of time.

679
00:42:39.308 --> 00:42:41.842
we are a free
and independent kingdom.

680
00:42:41.877 --> 00:42:43.844
The King in the North.

681
00:42:43.879 --> 00:42:46.346
All:
King in the North.

682
00:42:46.381 --> 00:42:47.948
Neither Joffrey
nor any of his men

683
00:42:47.983 --> 00:42:50.217
shall set foot
in our lands again.

684
00:42:50.285 --> 00:42:52.152
If he disregards
this command.

685
00:42:52.187 --> 00:42:55.723
he shall suffer
the same fate as my father.

686
00:42:55.757 --> 00:43:00.060
only I don't need a servant
to do my beheading for me.

687
00:43:00.094 --> 00:43:03.597
These are-- Your Grace.
these are--

688
00:43:03.631 --> 00:43:06.166
these are my terms.

689
00:43:06.200 --> 00:43:09.336
If the Queen Regent and her son
meet them. I'll give them peace.

690
00:43:09.370 --> 00:43:12.339
If not...

691
00:43:12.373 --> 00:43:14.808
I will litter the south
with Lannister dead.

692
00:43:14.843 --> 00:43:17.745
King Joffrey is a Baratheon.
Your Grace.

693
00:43:17.779 --> 00:43:19.580
Oh. is he?

694
00:43:20.783 --> 00:43:24.118
You'll ride at daybreak.
Ser Alton.

695
00:43:24.153 --> 00:43:26.787
That will be all
for tonight.

696
00:43:41.536 --> 00:43:43.671
A word. Your Grace?

697
00:43:45.440 --> 00:43:48.175
You don't have to call me
"Your Grace" when no one's around.

698
00:43:48.209 --> 00:43:50.912
It's not so bad
once you get used to it.

699
00:43:50.946 --> 00:43:52.780
I'm glad someone's
gotten used to it.

700
00:43:52.814 --> 00:43:56.150
The Lannisters are going to reject
your terms. you know?

701
00:43:56.184 --> 00:43:57.885
Of course they are.

702
00:43:57.919 --> 00:44:00.254
We can fight them
in the fields as long as you like.

703
00:44:00.288 --> 00:44:03.991
but we won't beat them until you
take King's Landing.

704
00:44:05.527 --> 00:44:08.663
And we can't take
King's Landing without ships.

705
00:44:08.697 --> 00:44:11.332
My father has ships and men
who know how to sail them.

706
00:44:11.367 --> 00:44:13.134
Men who fought
my father.

707
00:44:13.169 --> 00:44:15.603
Men who fought King Robert
to free themselves

708
00:44:15.637 --> 00:44:19.441
from the yoke of the South.
just like you're doing now.

709
00:44:20.609 --> 00:44:23.679
I'm his only living son.

710
00:44:23.713 --> 00:44:26.849
He'll listen to me.
I know he will.

711
00:44:29.285 --> 00:44:32.554
I'm not a Stark.
I know that.

712
00:44:32.589 --> 00:44:35.558
But your father raised me
to be an honorable man.

713
00:44:37.327 --> 00:44:39.829
We can avenge him
together.

714
00:44:41.131 --> 00:44:44.100
You don't want
Balon Greyjoy for an ally.

715
00:44:44.134 --> 00:44:46.402
I need his ships.
They say he has 200.

716
00:44:46.437 --> 00:44:50.006
They say a million rats
live in the sewers of King's Landing.

717
00:44:50.040 --> 00:44:51.975
Shall we rally them
to fight for us?

718
00:44:52.009 --> 00:44:53.843
I understand you don't
trust Lord Greyjoy.

719
00:44:53.878 --> 00:44:58.548
I don't trust Lord Greyjoy because
he is not trustworthy.

720
00:44:58.582 --> 00:45:01.217
Your father had to go to war
to end his rebellion.

721
00:45:01.252 --> 00:45:05.122
Yes. And now I'm the one
rebelling against the throne.

722
00:45:05.156 --> 00:45:07.424
Before me. it was father.

723
00:45:07.458 --> 00:45:09.125
You married one rebel
and mothered another.

724
00:45:09.159 --> 00:45:12.162
I mothered more than
just rebels.

725
00:45:12.196 --> 00:45:14.530
a fact you seem
to have forgotten.

726
00:45:14.565 --> 00:45:16.566
If I trade the Kingslayer
for two girls.

727
00:45:16.600 --> 00:45:18.867
my bannermen will string me up
by my feet.

728
00:45:18.902 --> 00:45:22.071
You want to leave Sansa
in the Queen's hands?

729
00:45:22.105 --> 00:45:24.173
<i>And Arya--</i>

730
00:45:24.207 --> 00:45:27.209
I haven't heard
a word about Arya.

731
00:45:27.244 --> 00:45:28.978
What are we fighting for
if not for them?

732
00:45:29.012 --> 00:45:30.613
It's more complicated
than that!

733
00:45:30.647 --> 00:45:32.782
You know it is.

734
00:45:47.232 --> 00:45:50.835
It's time for me
to go home.

735
00:45:50.869 --> 00:45:53.771
I haven't seen Bran
or Rickon in months.

736
00:45:54.740 --> 00:45:57.442
You can't go
to Winterfell.

737
00:45:57.476 --> 00:45:59.444
I beg your pardon?

738
00:45:59.478 --> 00:46:02.613
I'll send Rodrik
to watch over the boys

739
00:46:02.648 --> 00:46:07.184
because tomorrow
you'll ride south to the Stormlands.

740
00:46:07.218 --> 00:46:09.219
Why in the name
of all the Gods--

741
00:46:09.253 --> 00:46:13.156
because I need you to negotiate
with Renly Baratheon.

742
00:46:13.191 --> 00:46:15.325
He's rallied
an army of 100.000.

743
00:46:15.360 --> 00:46:17.094
You know him.
You know his family.

744
00:46:17.128 --> 00:46:19.562
I haven't seen Renly Baratheon
since he was a boy.

745
00:46:19.597 --> 00:46:21.131
<i>You have a hundred</i>
<i>other lords--</i>

746
00:46:21.165 --> 00:46:25.035
Which of these lords
do I trust more than you?

747
00:46:25.069 --> 00:46:27.871
If Renly sides with us.

748
00:46:27.906 --> 00:46:30.340
we'll outnumber them
two to one.

749
00:46:30.374 --> 00:46:33.310
When they feel the jaws beginning
to shut. they'll sue for peace.

750
00:46:33.344 --> 00:46:36.079
We'll get the girls back.

751
00:46:36.113 --> 00:46:39.616
Then we'll all
go home... for good.

752
00:46:46.724 --> 00:46:49.693
( Sighs )
I will ride at first light.

753
00:46:58.336 --> 00:47:01.938
We will all be together
again soon. I promise.

754
00:47:06.944 --> 00:47:09.545
You've done so well.

755
00:47:10.848 --> 00:47:14.717
Your father
would be... proud.

756
00:47:22.460 --> 00:47:25.462
- Give Lord Renly my regards.
- <i>King</i> Renly.

757
00:47:26.798 --> 00:47:29.567
There's a king
in every corner now.

758
00:47:31.303 --> 00:47:34.205
( Hammering )

759
00:47:42.514 --> 00:47:45.048
What is all this?

760
00:47:45.083 --> 00:47:47.351
Returning this room
to its proper appearance.

761
00:47:47.385 --> 00:47:50.253
Say what you will about the Targaryens--
they were conquerors.

762
00:47:50.288 --> 00:47:53.123
That is a seat
for a conqueror.

763
00:47:53.157 --> 00:47:56.826
It needs a room to match it.
not vines and flowers.

764
00:47:56.860 --> 00:47:59.228
We can't find Arya Stark.

765
00:47:59.263 --> 00:48:01.397
With luck. she's dead
in a ditch somewhere.

766
00:48:01.431 --> 00:48:03.399
Perhaps. But if not.
we need her.

767
00:48:03.433 --> 00:48:05.768
They'll never give Jaime back
to us for Sansa alone.

768
00:48:05.803 --> 00:48:08.404
I think they might.
They're weak.

769
00:48:08.439 --> 00:48:10.273
They put too much value
on their women.

770
00:48:10.307 --> 00:48:14.143
We need to set our armies
to the task of finding her.

771
00:48:14.178 --> 00:48:16.045
Send out as many men
as we can.

772
00:48:16.080 --> 00:48:17.881
I'm sure if you asked
grandfather--

773
00:48:17.915 --> 00:48:21.918
The King does not ask;
He commands.

774
00:48:21.952 --> 00:48:24.821
And my grandfather's
stupidity in the field of battle

775
00:48:24.855 --> 00:48:27.757
is the reason Robb Stark has
Uncle Jaime in the first place.

776
00:48:27.791 --> 00:48:30.492
His life is in danger.

777
00:48:30.527 --> 00:48:32.161
We're at war.

778
00:48:32.195 --> 00:48:35.296
All our lives
are in danger.

779
00:48:38.300 --> 00:48:41.803
I heard a disgusting lie
about Uncle Jaime.

780
00:48:41.837 --> 00:48:43.471
And you.

781
00:48:44.640 --> 00:48:46.141
Our enemies
will say anything

782
00:48:46.175 --> 00:48:48.176
to weaken your claim
to the throne.

783
00:48:48.211 --> 00:48:50.346
It's not a claim.
The throne is mine.

784
00:48:51.648 --> 00:48:53.750
Of course it is.

785
00:48:55.720 --> 00:48:57.621
No one believes
this foul gossip.

786
00:48:57.655 --> 00:48:59.790
Someone believes it.

787
00:49:01.126 --> 00:49:03.760
Father had
other children?

788
00:49:03.795 --> 00:49:06.330
Besides me and Tommen
and Myrcella?

789
00:49:08.133 --> 00:49:10.100
What are you asking?

790
00:49:10.134 --> 00:49:12.536
I'm asking if he fucked
other women

791
00:49:12.571 --> 00:49:14.105
when he grew tired
of you.

792
00:49:14.139 --> 00:49:15.940
How many bastards
does he have running--

793
00:49:15.974 --> 00:49:18.810
( silence )

794
00:49:24.316 --> 00:49:26.917
( Work resumes )

795
00:49:31.689 --> 00:49:35.925
What you just did
is punishable by death.

796
00:49:39.362 --> 00:49:42.064
You will never
do it again.

797
00:49:42.132 --> 00:49:44.033
Never.

798
00:49:50.073 --> 00:49:52.174
That will be all.
Mother.

799
00:49:56.413 --> 00:49:58.747
( Loud moaning )

800
00:49:58.782 --> 00:50:00.883
No. no. no. no.

801
00:50:00.918 --> 00:50:03.720
Do you have any idea
how ridiculous you sound?

802
00:50:03.754 --> 00:50:05.222
Ease into it.

803
00:50:05.256 --> 00:50:08.258
Slowly. with passion.

804
00:50:08.292 --> 00:50:12.029
( Moaning )
Oh. yeah.

805
00:50:12.064 --> 00:50:15.933
( Sighs ) Go wash yourselves.
Put some clothes on.

806
00:50:15.968 --> 00:50:18.570
Both of you
are working tonight.

807
00:50:22.340 --> 00:50:24.308
We do things
differently here. Daisy.

808
00:50:24.342 --> 00:50:28.311
This isn't some five-copper
bawdy house in Hayseed Hall.

809
00:50:28.345 --> 00:50:30.846
- Haystack Hall.
- Wherever you're from.

810
00:50:30.881 --> 00:50:32.715
Our establishment
doesn't cater

811
00:50:32.749 --> 00:50:35.517
to ploughmen
and goat herders.

812
00:50:35.551 --> 00:50:37.652
Lord Olsen.

813
00:50:37.686 --> 00:50:39.387
Taste is
everything here.

814
00:50:39.421 --> 00:50:41.289
Littlefinger's
a fancy man.

815
00:50:41.323 --> 00:50:43.091
Don't call him
Littlefinger.

816
00:50:43.126 --> 00:50:44.559
He doesn't like it.

817
00:50:44.594 --> 00:50:47.062
<i>Lord Baelish.</i>

818
00:50:52.269 --> 00:50:54.837
She pretends she doesn't
speak the common tongue

819
00:50:54.872 --> 00:50:57.440
so that people
will think she's exotic.

820
00:50:57.475 --> 00:51:00.377
She grew up just down the road
in flea bottom.

821
00:51:00.412 --> 00:51:02.980
She's beautiful.

822
00:51:03.014 --> 00:51:06.250
She's a dumb slut. really.
but a lid for every pot.

823
00:51:06.284 --> 00:51:07.951
<i>( Armor rattling )</i>

824
00:51:11.422 --> 00:51:13.624
Lord Commander.

825
00:51:13.658 --> 00:51:16.793
Good to see you...
Again.

826
00:51:21.799 --> 00:51:22.933
( Snaps fingers )

827
00:51:29.675 --> 00:51:31.476
- <i>( Door breaks )</i>
- <i>( Woman screams )</i>

828
00:51:31.510 --> 00:51:33.244
You do realize
this establishment

829
00:51:33.279 --> 00:51:35.614
is owned by
Lord Petyr Baelish.

830
00:51:35.649 --> 00:51:37.816
the King's
Master of Coin...

831
00:51:37.851 --> 00:51:39.785
Coin which goes
in many pockets.

832
00:51:39.820 --> 00:51:42.522
- Orders.
- Whose orders?

833
00:51:42.556 --> 00:51:45.557
Someone who doesn't care
what Littlefinger thinks.

834
00:51:45.592 --> 00:51:47.660
<i>( Patrons whispering )</i>

835
00:51:49.562 --> 00:51:52.331
( Whimpering. crying )

836
00:51:52.365 --> 00:51:55.634
( Baby crying )

837
00:52:03.175 --> 00:52:06.711
No. you can't.
No! Please!

838
00:52:06.746 --> 00:52:09.414
No! Not my Barra!

839
00:52:09.448 --> 00:52:12.851
- Please. Please.
- Enough. Get it done.

840
00:52:12.885 --> 00:52:14.919
- <i>Kill the bastard.</i>
- Mhaegen: <i>No. no!</i>

841
00:52:14.954 --> 00:52:17.455
- <i>Please.</i>
- Give it here.

842
00:52:17.490 --> 00:52:20.025
No. please.

843
00:52:20.059 --> 00:52:22.193
- <i>( Squelches )</i>
- ( Screaming )

844
00:52:29.935 --> 00:52:32.270
Man: <i>Spread out.</i>
<i>Search every house.</i>

845
00:52:32.304 --> 00:52:34.872
<i>Every room.</i>
<i>Look in every room.</i>

846
00:52:36.342 --> 00:52:38.910
( Grunting )

847
00:52:40.612 --> 00:52:43.747
( Women screaming )

848
00:52:48.253 --> 00:52:51.388
People shouting )

849
00:52:59.330 --> 00:53:01.831
Gendry!
His name is Gendry.

850
00:53:01.866 --> 00:53:03.733
Where is
the bastard?

851
00:53:03.767 --> 00:53:06.369
The Night's Watch!
Please. stop!

852
00:53:06.403 --> 00:53:07.770
Where?

853
00:53:07.804 --> 00:53:10.773
They took him up the Kingsroad.
heading north.

854
00:53:10.807 --> 00:53:14.409
- How will we know him?
- <i>He's got a bull's head helmet.</i>

855
00:53:14.443 --> 00:53:17.678
- <i>He made it himself.</i>
- Find him.

856
00:53:51.747 --> 00:53:54.416
<i>( Theme music playing )</i>

857
00:53:54.441 --> 00:53:58.441
== sync. corrected by <font color="#00ff00">elderman</font> ==

9999
00:00:0.500 --> 00:00:2.00
